cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use laya-micro, please cite it as below."
title: laya-micro
abstract: >-
  A toolkit for shrinking Convai Innovations' Laya typed-decision model so it
  runs on single-board computers. It combines a BPE-merge-closed vocabulary
  prune with block-wise int8 ONNX quantization, and evaluates the result on
  human-labelled robot commands, reporting majority-class baselines and
  per-class precision and recall alongside accuracy.
type: software
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Glago
    given-names: Gideon
    alias: osamabinIaggin
    country: GH
# TODO: confirm this URL once laya-micro is pushed.
repository-code: "https://github.com/osamabinIaggin/laya-micro"
# TODO: add `version:` and `date-released: YYYY-MM-DD` at the first tagged release.
keywords:
  - laya
  - typed decisions
  - model compression
  - vocabulary pruning
  - quantization
  - onnx
  - raspberry-pi
  - edge-inference
  - robotics
